node_modules/
dist/
*.log
.DS_Store
# Rendered media is committed; the rest of `.reel-cache/` is not.
#
# `voiceCacheDir()` calls the voice cache "committed, so renders reproduce", and
# `reel doctor` tells you a render needs no key because "narration renders from
# the committed voice cache". Neither was true: this file ignored the whole
# directory, so the mp3s never left the machine that synthesized them and a
# narrated spec was reproducible only for its author.
#
# Committing them is what makes narration and diagrams deterministic. Each is a
# pure function of its cache key — voice, model, style and text for a spoken
# line; source and theme for a diagram — so a checkout renders the same words in
# the same voice and the same flowchart with no API key, no mermaid install, no
# browser, no spend, and no drift when a provider or a library changes what it
# produces for unchanged input.
#
# A negation cannot re-include anything under an excluded directory, hence
# `/*` on the parent rather than the bare directory.
**/.reel-cache/*
!**/.reel-cache/voice/
!**/.reel-cache/diagram/
.reel-out/
coverage/
*.tsbuildinfo
.env
.env.local
scripts/out/
scripts/authored.reel.yaml
examples/*/out/
demos/out/
# Planning notes kept alongside the code but not published with it: the
# positioning, competitive read and roadmap are working documents, not docs.
/demosascodeproductplan*.md

# Renders written by a spec's `output:` paths when run from the repo root
# (hero.reel.yaml, aangan.reel.yaml). The copies the site ships are committed
# under studio/public/demo/ instead — see docs/deploy-site.md.
/out/

# Diagnostics from a failed step — local, never committed.
.reel-failures/

# The render fingerprint is committed, not ignored.
#
# It is what `record --if-changed` compares against, and a fresh checkout with
# no stamp answers "no previous render recorded" — so the flag never skipped
# anything in CI, which is the one place it was meant to save time. It also
# carries the caption timeline `reel review` needs to spot a caption the screen
# no longer matches.
#
# Safe to commit because it is a pure function of the render: no timestamp, and
# its paths are relative to itself. Identical inputs write identical bytes.

# Before/after strips from `reel diff` — a review aid, not an artifact.
.reel-diff/

# Saved sign-ins. A Playwright storage state holds live session cookies — a
# bearer credential, not config — so committing one signs everybody in as you.
# `reel capture --save-auth` writes these, and warns when git can still see them.
.auth/
*.storagestate.json
storage-state*.json
auth.json
*-auth.json
